	(text_box "Component Value Notes:\n- Original simulation done with R17 = 100 ohms\n  and C17 = 220pF. Good attentuation noticed but \n  a little more attenuation would be better so \n  the R and C values were increased to a common\n  value around 2 times higher for each.\n- Second implementation (using PWL w/ V for ESD spike): \n	Max V(tvs diode) = 8kV @ 0.7ns\n	Max V(c17) = 38.38V @ 1ns (still too high? or would tau for the next RC combination ensure the high voltage doesn't hit the op amp and mcu?)\n- For R17: 220ohms and C17:470pF\n  -3dB frequency = 1.531MHz\n- Simulation Directory: GitHub\\nucleo-g474re-audio-board\\AnalogPathDesign\\ESDSpikeProtectionDesign\\LTspice\\\nVinpp_1_25_V_Vtran_8kV_R220_C470p\\Vtran_8kV_R220_C470p.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 80.01 0)
		(size 92.71 31.75)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.0254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 253 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "43d6921e-5414-40a3-bdfa-2fdc4be709ba")
	)
	(text_box "Voltage Divider Notes: \n- The purpose of this voltage divider is to attenuate the amplitude of the input from the 3.5 mm line-in signal in the case it is beyond the range of our ADC (0V to 3.3V).\n- There is no one standard peak-to-peak value that all audio outputs on devices use. While apple's official specs fortheir DAC's are hard to find, other sources online mention line-out Vpp specs as anywhere from 1Vpp to 5Vpp. We are assuming and recommending no one tries to use a 30Vpp line-out signal from pro audio equipment as a line-in input.\n- Following the information found online, a 50% voltage divider is deemed appropriate so as to not attenuate a 1Vpp input signal too much and to attenuate a 5vpp signal just enough to still be able to use most of the ADC's range.\n- Referenced sources from Cirrus Logic below due to Cirrus Logic being a dependable reference for standards in DACs. \n- Simulation Directory: \nGitHub\\nucleo-g474re-audio-board\\\nAnalogPathDesign\\VoltageDivider\\\nVin_2_5_vpp_100Hz_Vout_halfVin.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 114.3 80.01 0)
		(size 67.31 41.91)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.0254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 253 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6aaad0d6-c9db-46a7-b2bf-16ca2d30e412")
	)
	(text_box "DC Blocker Notes:\n- The purpose of the DC Blocker is to remove any unintended DC offset voltages from the line-in signal before we apply the intended offset for the ADC.\n- Simulation Directory: GitHub\\nucleo-g474re-audio-board\\\nAnalogPathDesign\\DCBlocker\\Vin_2_5_Vpp_100Hz_VinRef_2V_VoutRef_0V.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 182.88 80.01 0)
		(size 73.66 15.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.0254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 253 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7fd0bb7f-ccc0-4024-97eb-ad39eef3e55c")
	)
